      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Box breathing actively engages your parasympathetic nervous system, which is your body's \"rest and digest\" state. This controlled pattern signals to your brain that you are safe, directly counteracting the stress response. In doing so, it helps lower heart rate and reduces the production of stress hormones like cortisol. Consistent practice can train your nervous system to become less reactive to stressors.",
